{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And afterward the people journeyed from Hazeroth and camped in the wilderness of Paran\"</b> is to say that when they journeyed from Hazeroth, they did not travel from this wilderness to a different wilderness, as in the first journey when they set out from the wilderness of Sinai and camped in the wilderness of Paran (Numbers 10:12), but rather they journeyed from Hazeroth, which is in the wilderness of Paran, and camped in another place within that same wilderness, namely Kadesh-barnea. For from there the spies were sent, as it says in another place: \"to the wilderness of Paran, to Kadesh\" (Numbers 13:26), and so it is written: \"And we came to Kadesh-barnea, etc. And you came near to me and said, 'Let us send men'\" (Deuteronomy 1:19–22). And Scripture did not say \"they journeyed from Hazeroth and camped in Kadesh-barnea,\" because there were perhaps many stations between them and there is no place to mention them now, but it mentioned the wilderness of Paran to make known that this Kadesh is Kadesh-barnea, which is in the wilderness of Paran, not the Kadesh that is in the wilderness of Zin, where the matter of the waters of Meribah took place in the fortieth year."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:35.994641473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}